1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,513
The use case says what the IDM is for, who takes part, and where and when it applies.

2
00:00:06,413 --> 00:00:07,452
Open the use case.

3
00:00:07,452 --> 00:00:10,338
Write a short summary of the information exchange.

4
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:16,426
Under aim and scope, state the purpose and what is out of scope.

5
00:00:17,663 --> 00:00:18,436
Add the use.

6
00:00:18,436 --> 00:00:23,401
Choose User-defined Use, type Construction Quality Management, and click Add.

7
00:00:23,401 --> 00:00:26,431
You can also pick a use from the NBIMS-US list.

8
00:00:27,331 --> 00:00:30,997
Select the target region, Korea, and remove International.

9
00:00:30,997 --> 00:00:32,515
The language is English.

10
00:00:33,415 --> 00:00:38,809
Under actor roles, the blank project already has one actor, linked to its pool.

11
00:00:38,809 --> 00:00:40,790
Rename it General contractor.

12
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:44,067
Click Sub-actor: the pool is divided into lanes.

13
00:00:44,067 --> 00:00:47,687
Name them Site quality inspector and BIM coordinator.

14
00:00:48,587 --> 00:00:51,736
Click Add Actor for the owner's representative.

15
00:00:51,736 --> 00:00:53,880
The app also adds a pool for it.

16
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:59,509
Tick External: it receives the daily report, but its own process is outside the IDM.

17
00:01:00,409 --> 00:01:05,121
Finally, tick the ISO 22263 project phase, production.

18
00:01:05,121 --> 00:01:14,980
The catch-up file DMBCF_5b_use_case.idm contains the complete use case, with all actors, keywords and references.

